# The boreutils tree M-PX3 runs (px12; tools/mkboreutils builds it).
#
# boreutils trunk at the time of px12 (2026-10-07): 2f15585, pinned in
# its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.23 / lupin 0.1.46 / wolf-std
# 6a0df5e. tools/mkboreutils builds it with THAT toolchain (the archive
# by the digest boreutils names, the std tree at the commit it names),
# not with kernel/wolf.pin's: the binaries are boreutils' own, built
# from boreutils' own tree.
#
# px15 (2026-10-08) moves it to boreutils trunk 50d8907: bu17's pin
# (wolf 0.2.25 / lupin 0.1.48 / wolf-std 0f74ec5) and bu18's `ls`, so
# /bin/ls is boreutils' and busybox leaves the initramfs.
#
# px26 (2026-10-11) moves it to boreutils trunk 870815c (bu20): bu19's
# and bu20's pins (wolf 0.2.27 / lupin 0.1.50, the std the tree names)
# and bu20's `ls -l` and family, `stat`, `readlink` and `env`, which
# join the shell's /bin. Its `cat` copies with `copy_file_range` and
# `sendfile` (bu19), and its long listing reads /etc/passwd,
# /etc/group and /etc/localtime.
#
# px27 (2026-10-11) moves it to boreutils trunk abc59f5 (bu21): the same
# toolchain (wolf 0.2.27 / lupin 0.1.50) and bu21's `mkdir`, `rmdir`,
# `rm`, `mv` and `cp`, 36 utilities in all.
#
# px36 (2026-10-12) moves it to boreutils trunk 2ab3651 (bu22): wolf
# 0.2.28 / lupin 0.1.51 / wolf-std 98e1b7b, and bu22's `chmod`, `touch`
# and `ln`, `mkdir -m` and `cp -p`, 39 utilities in all.
#
# px46 (2026-10-15) moves it to boreutils trunk 23ea8dd (bu24): wolf
# 0.2.30 / lupin 0.1.53 / wolf-std fd6bcdc, bu23's `kill` and bu24's
# `id`, `whoami`, `groups`, `logname`, `chown` and `chgrp`, 46 utilities
# in all. No existing utility's source moved (bu23 and bu24 add files).
#
# px49 (2026-10-17) moves it to boreutils trunk 8f0bbb1 (bu25,
# boreutils#35): `cat` refuses an input that is its output by GNU's
# measured rule (src/cat.lu, src/bore/inout.lu: on Linux it asks
# /proc/self/fd/1 and /proc/self/fdinfo/1). PAX lists /proc/<pid>/fd but
# a lookup of an entry is -ENOENT, so on PAX the check finds nothing and
# refuses nothing: the refusal is dark here (recorded, notes/px49). No
# other utility's source moved; the same wolf-toolchain.toml.
#
# px51 (2026-10-18) moves it to boreutils trunk 43ee185 (bu27): wolf
# 0.2.32 / lupin 0.1.54 / wolf-std d37c911, `kill` reaching process
# groups (`kill -- -PGID`, `kill 0` as `getpgrp` then the group, `kill
# -1`; `-l`/`-t` with the host's whole numbering) and the new `timeout`
# (its command in timeout's own group unless --foreground, the group
# sent to at expiry), 47 utilities in all; `sleep`'s duration parsing
# moved to src/bore/duration.lu, which `timeout` shares. bu27's static
# release kill is 0f4fb3b7… and timeout de9104db….
#
# px53 (2026-10-20) moves it to boreutils trunk cc64f68 (bu28; src/ is
# 18a6490's): wolf 0.2.33 / lupin 0.1.54 / wolf-std cceda63, the four
# refusals retired (boreutils#41): `timeout -s SEGV`, `-s RTMIN` and a
# host number ignore the signal, then send it to the group (a command
# still in the group, read from /proc/PID/stat, is sent it once, by the
# group send), a command dead of a signal leaves timeout dead of it
# (`os_exit_signal`), `the monitored command dumped core` from wait4's
# core bit, `kill -t`/`-L`'s row 0 (`Unknown signal 0`). bu28's static
# release kill is b0e45268… and timeout 245f8414… (pax d6fbcdc's
# tools/mkboreutils, this file's since).
BORE_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/boreutils
BORE_REV=cc64f687420961228c415e117ba5bb97d5624836
